// `~`, `&`, `|`, `<<` and `>>` all existed; `^` scanned as an unexpected
// character. It binds between `|` and `&`, which is Python's ordering.
println(6 ^ 3)
println(0 ^ 0)
println(6 ^ 3 == 5)
println(1 | 6 ^ 3 & 2)
// The bitwise operators have no compound assignment form, and `^` does not
// gain one on its own.
println(12 ^ 10)
